LOGBOOK.md-14-### 1454 — libssh2 adapter review rework closes async ownership gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md-15-- ROOT CAUSE: Actor isolation serialized synchronous libssh2 calls but not the socket service work awaited between `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` retries. Reentrant progress calls could snapshot the same outbound prefix, issue duplicate writes, and later remove inconsistent byte counts; suspended operations also retained channel/session pointers while teardown could free them.
LOGBOOK.md-16-- REWORK: Socket progress now has one queued owner with exact-once partial drains. Channel reads enforce one pending operation per stream, writes reserve against the per-channel queued-byte cap, all pending gauges are live, and cancel/reset/close marks disposition then waits for tracked pointer users before bounded free. Session/open/connect teardown paths similarly drain active owners and serialize concurrent teardown.
