LOGBOOK.md-21-### 0351 — Pinned libssh2 adapter joins the macOS provider and harness graphs (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md-22-- IMPLEMENTATION: `ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` is the sole Swift target importing the pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL XCFramework. A serialized transport actor drives custom send/receive callbacks in nonblocking mode over the injected `SSHTCPConnection`; bounded async bridges turn socket and external-Keychain-signer progress into `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` without blocking a provider executor.
LOGBOOK.md:23:- SECURITY: The adapter applies explicit KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC allowlists with no SHA-1/CBC fallback, delivers the exact raw host-key blob plus negotiated host-key method and canonical SHA-256 fingerprint to policy before credential lookup, and carries only opaque credential references/public signing material across Core. Engine prose and endpoint/user/command data never enter errors or typed diagnostics.
LOGBOOK.md-24-- DECISION: Consumer-driven receive credit, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit presence/`coreDumped`, and deep server-KEX/keepalive reporting are all emitted as `unsupported`, owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`. Client rekey, server-rekey protocol handling, bounded channel I/O, exec/stdin upload, and forced `keepalive@openssh.com` transmission remain implemented M0 behavior; no unavailable value is inferred from libssh2 internals.
LOGBOOK.md-25-- ANOMALY: Xcode's generated package scheme copied both library-style XCFramework module maps to one custom `Release/include/module.modulemap`, producing a deterministic multiple-producer error once the libssh2 and native-fixture graphs met. The Apple matrix now keeps Xcode's existing device/simulator/native checks and uses isolated dual-architecture SwiftPM builds with `-application-extension` for the macOS provider/harness; the stripped release harness check verifies libssh2's intentionally hidden local rekey symbol separately from exported HEV symbols.
LOGBOOK.md-26-- VERIFICATION: Strict recursive Swift format lint, `make validate-core` (345 tests/30 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, pinned-source tamper gates, and the revised Apple matrix all exit 0. Focused adapter tests cover bounded partial transport I/O, oversized-read rejection, async signer EAGAIN, explicit deferred capability states, and 20 repeated failed handshakes returning sessions/channels/sockets/tasks/custom allocations/buffers to zero.
