LOGBOOK.md-189-### 0755 — An exhaustive entitlement allowlist inherits every entitlement the architecture implies, including ones the matrix only mentioned in prose (TASK-260715-ypo7yo, r3)
LOGBOOK.md-190-- ROOT CAUSE: r2 argued in D-4 that `ReluxProxyMac` is sandboxed *because of* Sparkle, and quoted the spec clause naming the `-spks`/`-spki` Mach lookup exceptions — then never authored `com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name` as an entitlement row. The r2 containment assertion A10b declares every present key must be authored or signing-generated, so the allowlist would have **rejected a correctly built sandboxed Sparkle host**. Same defect class as r1's F3, one revision later: prose acknowledged the requirement, the machine-checkable set did not. The generalisable lesson is that the moment an assertion becomes *exhaustive*, every architectural consequence stated anywhere in the contract must also appear as data — rationale text is no longer a place a requirement can live.
