LOGBOOK.md:857:- DECISION: Both engine adapters use one serialized, type-erased `ReluxTunnelCore` boundary with mandatory raw host-key policy evaluation before credential access, bounded partial writes, independent byte-stream halves, capped observable per-channel receive credit, automatic byte/time plus explicit/server rekey, keepalive, stable errors, schema-v1 metrics/events, and privacy-safe opaque lane identity. ADR-014 remains open; unsupported mandatory behavior is a red matrix row, never a candidate-specific skip.
LOGBOOK.md-858-- FINDING: The existing `SSHContracts.swift` is intentionally only an M0 boundary skeleton and no board item owned implementation of the reviewed semantic surface before both adapters and the common suite. Created atomic TASK-260720-100wu6 and linked it between this contract and TASK-260715-1af33i, TASK-260715-1ozsb6, and TASK-260715-2d3g5e; the independent NIOSSH fork continues to consume this contract directly.
LOGBOOK.md-859-- VERIFICATION: The contract defines every operation, state, timeout/cancellation scope, error, metric, privacy rule, and E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-BACKPRESSURE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY/E-KEEPALIVE/E-CANCEL/E-SCALE/E-ERRORS/E-METRICS-PRIVACY/E-INJECTION row. Three task-scoped PlantUML sources pass syntax checking and their lifecycle, pre-auth host verification, and channel/window/rekey SVG renders were visually inspected.
