LOGBOOK.md-861-### 0812 — Review: SSH engine audit accepted after full independent fact-check (TASK-260715-28ok1k)
LOGBOOK.md-862-- MILESTONE: Audit accepted → `done`. Every load-bearing claim reproduced from upstream: tag→commit pins for both candidates plus all six transitive deps (ls-remote), all three archive SHA-256 and both license hashes (fresh downloads), 16 MiB window `SSHChannelMultiplexer.swift:211`, internal `_rekey()` `NIOSSHHandler.swift:511`, libssh2 window APIs and direct-tcpip hardcode `src/channel.c:384,457`, unexported reexchange `src/packet.c:1369`, version-macro anomaly, six CVE fix commits confirmed ancestors of `a343024`, GHSA advisories via API, exactly 679 libssh2 commits/12mo.
--
LOGBOOK.md-878-- REWORK: The loopback listener fd is closed exactly once by its dispatch-source cancel handler on `listenerQueue`; `stop()` waits for cancellation before returning, eliminating the accept-loop fd-reuse window.
LOGBOOK.md-879-- VERIFICATION: Strict swift-format, 49 Swift tests, `swift build`, 8 HEV tests under ThreadSanitizer, and `make validate-native` all pass. The residual quit-vs-spontaneous-return race remains upstream-inherent and would require a forbidden HEV patch; the return guard narrows exposure to that concurrent window.
